  "question": {
    "text": "If $[x]$ denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$, then the value of the integral $\\int_{0}^{2} x^{2}[x] d x$ equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MYCQy",
      "text": "$\\frac{5}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aOk9z",
      "text": "$\\frac{7}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FGjao",
      "text": "$\\frac{8}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OAqgg",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let.\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nI &=\\int_{0}^{2} x^{2}[x] d x \\\\\r\n&=\\int_{0}^{1} x^{2} \\cdot 0 d x+\\int_{1}^{2} x^{2} \\times 1 d x \\\\\r\n&=\\left[\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right]_{1}^{2}=\\left[\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right]=\\frac{7}{3}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
